e7cae80ae3d6e\nSIGNAL: f0c38d24fd53e1ff8350bbfd06951cf70c9ddc21ed2110829fd8e48e000d85b8\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Orchard\nbiologics facility:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning with exactly\n   `# Orchard Evidence and Decision Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning with exactly\n   `# Orchard Biologics Restart Decision` and containing exactly these ordered\n   level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and restart states`\n   2. `Process, genealogy, and hold-time controls`\n   3. `Aseptic, analytical, and cold-chain release gates`\n   4. `Utilities, materials, staffing, and staged restart`\n   5. `Cybersecurity, telemetry, and evidence custody`\n   6. `Safety, environmental, and communication continuity`\n   7. `Execution, rollback, and contingencies`\n   8. `Verification, blockers, falsifiers, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,400–1,900 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. It must reconcile\nauthority, process performance, aseptic controls, cold-chain excursion,\nutilities, analytical disposition, cybersecurity, materials/staffing,\nenvironmental duties, monitoring, communications, candidate lineage, and\nindependent readiness.\n\nDo not merely list facts. Bind every action and gate to owners, prerequisites,\nobservations, current candidate/version, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that\nretires temporary controls. Preserve exact distinctions including observations\nversus gates, alert versus action limits, installed versus usable capacity,\npercent versus probability, hours versus days, source-local authority, and\ncurrent versus stale evidence.\n\nThe task-native artifacts are exact cumulative work. Checks are candidate-bound\nmechanical feedback and do not independently authorize lot release, commercial\nrestart, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-005 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:SAFETY:1-64+SIGNAL:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"b55ca512d2baa7dcf636e3b7324187193f3b05488fdea16b60f5ebb5ba6aa60c\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-005\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SAFETY\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SIGNAL\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7644}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"SAFETY\",\"source_path\":\"sources/SAFETY_ENVIRONMENT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"163e6d198789dc487419a4149aea6b41ec06976a16b57924f51e7cae80ae3d6e\",\"source_size_bytes\":3423,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Worker safety, emissions, waste, and notification\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nA material unauthorized solvent release requires initial notice within twenty-four hours of determination, not twenty-four minutes after detection.\nTemporary neutralization may proceed under permit condition N-12, but discharge above 0.021 milligrams per liter at the outfall requires an immediate stop.\nDetermination evidence, notices, candidate changes, checks, and closure records must be retained for seven years with access provenance.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSIGNAL supplies alarm evidence and CURRENT supplies utility state. CHARTER owns materiality determination; a semantic record cannot make the legal determination.\nCOMMUNE supplies notice-delivery records and GUARD protects sensitive facility details.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| ENV-000 | solvent-room | v3 | 24.0 | hours | superseded |\n| ENV-001 | waste-tank | v3 | 25.7 | hours | c